Looking at the `ChatFileList` component usage, I need to check if files exist and display them in red if not found. I'll update the `ChatFileList` component to verify file existence via the API.

```vue client/src/components/chat/ChatFileList.vue
<script setup>
import { API } from '../../api/api'
</script>

<template>
  <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1 items-center">
    <div
      v-for="file in fileStatuses"
      :key="file.path"
      class="flex items-center gap-1 px-2 py-1 rounded text-xs cursor-pointer"
      :class="fileChipClass(file)"
      :title="file.exists === false ? 'File not found: ' + file.path : file.path"
    >
      <i class="fa-solid fa-file text-xs"></i>
      <span>{{ file.label }}</span>
      <div class="flex gap-1 ml-1">
        <i
          v-if="canAddAsMessage(file)"
          class="fa-solid fa-comment text-xs opacity-60 hover:opacity-100"
          title="Add as message"
          @click.stop="$emit('add-as-message', file.path)"
        ></i>
        <i
          v-if="isNotebook(file)"
          class="fa-solid fa-rotate text-xs opacity-60 hover:opacity-100"
          title="Sync notebook"
          @click.stop="$emit('sync-notebook', file.path)"
        ></i>
        <i
          v-if="isNotebook(file)"
          class="fa-solid fa-file-export text-xs opacity-60 hover:opacity-100"
          title="Export notebook"
          @click.stop="$emit('export-notebook', file.path)"
        ></i>
        <i
          class="fa-solid fa-xmark text-xs opacity-60 hover:opacity-100"
          title="Remove"
          @click.stop="$emit('remove', file.path)"
        ></i>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  props: ['files'],
  emits: ['remove', 'add-as-message', 'sync-notebook', 'export-notebook'],
  data() {
    return {
      // Map of file path -> { path, label, exists: true|false|null }
      fileStatuses: []
    }
  },
  watch: {
    files: {
      immediate: true,
      handler(files) {
        this.syncFiles(files)
      }
    }
  },
  methods: {
    // Sync file list and trigger existence checks for new entries
    syncFiles(files) {
      if (!files) { this.fileStatuses = []; return }
      const existing = new Map(this.fileStatuses.map(f => [f.path, f]))
      this.fileStatuses = files.map(path => {
        if (existing.has(path)) return existing.get(path)
        const entry = { path, label: path.split('/').reverse()[0], exists: null }
        this.checkFileExists(entry)
        return entry
      })
    },

    // Check file existence via API and update entry reactively
    async checkFileExists(entry) {
      try {
        await API.files.read(entry.path)
        entry.exists = true
      } catch {
        entry.exists = false
      }
    },

    fileChipClass(file) {
      if (file.exists === false) {
        return 'bg-error/20 text-error border border-error/40'
      }
      if (file.exists === null) {
        return 'bg-base-200 text-base-content/60 border border-base-300'
      }
      return 'bg-base-200 text-base-content border border-base-300 hover:bg-base-300'
    },

    isNotebook(file) {
      return file.path?.endsWith('.ipynb')
    },

    canAddAsMessage(file) {
      return file.exists !== false
    }
  }
}
</script>
```

Key changes:
- **`fileStatuses`** array tracks each file with `{ path, label, exists }` where `exists` is `null` (loading), `true`, or `false`
- **`checkFileExists`** calls `API.files.read()` — if it throws, the file doesn't exist
- **`fileChipClass`** returns red (`text-error` / `bg-error`) styling when `exists === false`, neutral grey while loading, and normal style when found
- Files not found show a tooltip with the full path and the "Add as message" action is hidden
- Watches `files` prop with `syncFiles` to avoid re-checking already-resolved entries

